# Template for the local development environment.
#
#   1. Copy this file to `.env` — `.env` is git-ignored and never published:
#        cp .env.example .env
#   2. Fill in your own password.
#
# Docker Compose reads `.env` automatically from this folder and passes
# MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD to the SQL Server container. Use the SAME password in the
# backend user-secrets (README -> Local development -> Run the backend).
#
# SQL Server password policy: at least 8 characters, using three of the four
# categories: uppercase, lowercase, digits, symbols.
#
# The value is intentionally EMPTY: docker-compose enforces that the password is
# set, so a copy of this file can never start a database with a known password.
MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD=
